WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:08.680
What does the coup mean for United States
and Turkey relations?

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.710
You know, there's going to be a real rough
patch coming soon.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:17.260
Turkish media, which is pretty much all state
controlled at this point, has basically said

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.820
that the United States had some complicity
in this.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:25.160
The reason for that conspiracy, which is nonsense,
is because Fethullah Gulen, a Pennsylvania-based

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.240
cleric who's an exile from Turkey, has been
accused by Recep Tayyip Erdogan of leading

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.240
this.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.940
There's not much evidence there, but Erdogan
is demanding that the United States extradite

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:35.940
this cleric.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.610
And if we do extradite him, he might ultimately
face the death penalty inside Turkey.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:46.030
Now, this is reminiscent back in 1979 when
Ayatollah Khomeini demanded that the Carter

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:51.390
administration extradite the Shah, who like
Gulen, was in the United States for medical

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.680
treatment.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:58.120
Declassified Soviet documents show that Carter's
willingness to do that, he exiled the Shah

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.649
to Panama, ended up being a factor in the
Soviet Union deciding that the United States

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:07.750
was too weak to counter the Afghan invasion.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.040
So what will the coup mean for US-Turkey relations?

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.180
Let us know in the comments, and let us know
any other topics you'd like AEI scholars to

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.789
address in 60 seconds.

